Another game that used a system like this was Dungeon Master, around the mid
to late 80s. It might be worth taking a look at as the game was very much
like nethack in some ways.

In the other area of the thread I was talking about how hard the original
idea would be, but this would be a great way to implement it in a small way.
You could put as many syllables in as you wanted and if you made them random
it wouldn't be easy to figure out.



